und. In addition, multiple rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms are expected Wednesday afternoon through Thursday\nevening producing periods of heavy rainfall and potential flash\nflooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-18T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3cf39aa90455238aaed4fdb23ced03f0914e3184.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3cf39aa90455238aaed4fdb23ced03f0914e3184.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-16T00:17:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 160017 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 617 PM MDT Tue Sep 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - There is a chance for strong to severe storms over the next few days, capable of producing hail, gusty winds, and heavy rainfall. - Moderate to heavy rainfall could lead to localized flash flooding, rockfalls, and mudslides at times this week. - Flood Watc","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-15T19:00:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Critical fire weather conditions will not be met as subtropical moisture continues to feed into the 4 Corners and Central Rockies region this week. Daily and nightly shower and thunderstorm activity can be anticipated with some storms producing gusty outflow winds and containing moderate to heavy rainfall rates. Widespread wetting rainfall appears likely through the week. ...GUSTY ER","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"ctz01","station_name":"Cortez","distance_km":5.4,"soil_temp_5cm_f":66.63,"soil_temp_15cm_f":66.04,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar